            core: "A Fabric lakehouse combines data lake scalability with data warehouse query capabilities, storing structured, semi-structured, and unstructured data in OneLake and offering both Apache Spark (read/write) and a read-only SQL analytics endpoint.",
            tech: "<ul><li>Areas: Tables (managed Delta tables) and Files (unstructured/non-Delta data like JSON, Parquet, images, documents). Placing data in Tables auto-validates, extracts metadata, and registers the table in the Hive metastore.</li><li>Access paths: Spark (Python, Scala, SQL, R) for read/write; SQL analytics endpoint for read-only T-SQL queries</li><li>Storage format: Delta Lake (Parquet with transaction log)</li><li>Schema management: Schema-on-read with optional enforcement through Delta</li><li>Transaction support: Single-table ACID through Delta Lake only; no multi-table transactions</li><li>Write support: Spark notebooks, pipelines, dataflows, Spark job definitions</li><li>Read support: Spark + T-SQL via SQL analytics endpoint; Power BI via Direct Lake mode</li><li>Data types: Structured, semi-structured (JSON, Parquet), unstructured (images, documents)</li><li>AI integration: Spark MLlib, scikit-learn run natively; Semantic Link (SemPy) bridges Power BI semantic models and lakehouse data; vector embeddings stored as Delta tables for RAG/similarity search; Files area stores documents/images for generative AI pipelines</li><li>Limitations: Batch or micro-batch only (not real-time streaming); no full DDL/DML on SQL analytics endpoint (read-only); no multi-table ACID transactions</li></ul>",
            gotchas: "SQL analytics endpoint is read-only: no DDL/DML. Single-table vs. multi-table ACID: Lakehouse provides single-table ACID via Delta; warehouse provides multi-table ACID via T-SQL. Direct Lake on lakehouse falls back to DirectQuery if the query exceeds memory/resource thresholds. Auto-registration: Files placed in Tables are automatically registered as Delta tables; files placed in Files are not."
