            tech: "<ul><li>Architecture: A workspace of KQL databases sharing capacity and resources</li><li>Data types: Time-series, event-based, semi-structured (JSON, text), structured</li><li>Primary query language: Kusto Query Language (KQL); also supports a subset of T-SQL</li><li>Write support: Streaming ingestion, batch ingestion, Eventstream, SDKs, Kafka, Logstash, dataflows</li><li>Read support: KQL, T-SQL (subset), Power BI via DirectQuery (not Direct Lake)</li><li>Storage format: Columnar store with automatic indexing and compression</li><li>Schema management: Schema-on-write with dynamic fields for semi-structured data</li><li>Transaction support: Append-optimized; not designed for UPDATE/DELETE operations</li><li>Partitioning: Automatic time-based partitioning and indexing by ingestion time</li><li>Always-On option: Available for time-sensitive systems that cannot tolerate startup latency; stays available continuously and scales via autoscale</li><li>AI integration: Built-in KQL ML functions: series_decompose_anomalies for anomaly detection, series_decompose_forecast for time-series forecasting, make-series for time-series analysis; real-time scoring pipelines via Eventstream</li><li>High-volume ingestion: Optimized for millions of events per day; queryable within seconds</li></ul>",
